  "p1_findings": [
    {
      "id": "P1_NONATOMIC_DUAL_RECEIPT_PUBLICATION_CAN_FALSE_PASS",
      "evidence": "m519_r14_record_output_artifacts is invoked in an OR-list. Under Bash this suppresses errexit inside the function. The two final mv -T commands are sequential and unchecked. Precreating artifact_inventory.tsv as a directory makes rm -f and the first mv fail, but the second mv publishes artifact_terminal_receipt.txt and returns zero. Independent replay observed helper_rc=0 with inventory still a directory and terminal status PASS_M519_R14_COMPLETE_REGULAR_NONSYMLINK_OUTPUT_TUPLE.",
      "impact": "The unique DC run may emit RUN_COMPLETE even though the promised inventory/terminal receipt pair is incomplete. This directly contradicts the candidate's atomic-receipt claim.",
      "required_repair": "Create a fresh additive source identity. Make every cleanup, write, fsync-equivalent validation and publish operation explicitly fail-closed independent of errexit context. Prefer one staging receipt directory containing both files and a single atomic directory rename; otherwise chain both publishes with explicit checked returns, then require both published paths to be regular non-symlink nonempty and cross-consistent before RUN_COMPLETE. Add both destination-directory partial-publication attacks to the built-in no-EDA tests."
    },
    {
      "id": "P1_ANCESTOR_SYMLINK_AND_POST_RECEIPT_TOCTOU_BYTES_ESCAPE_SEAL_CLOSURE",
      "evidence": "The helper rejects only leaf symlinks. With point/netlist as a symlink to an external directory, all three leaf tests pass and the terminal says PASS, while the runner's find-based seal contains zero mapped-v/mapped-sdc/ddc files. A second replay changed the DDC after receipt publication but before RUN_COMPLETE/sealing; the outer seal verified and RUN_COMPLETE existed although the receipt DDC SHA differed from the final sealed DDC SHA.",
      "impact": "A nominally sealed result can name artifact bytes that are not inside the sealed tree, or can seal bytes different from those named by the artifact receipts. The package therefore does not yet close artifact identity through final sealing.",
      "required_repair": "Reject symlink ancestors for point and netlist and require resolved artifact paths to remain beneath the exact regular work/axis directory. After publishing RUN_COMPLETE, cross-validate both receipts against the three live artifacts and against the enclosing SHA256SUMS immediately before canonical publication; require the manifest to contain exactly the three expected artifact paths with the same SHA values. Add ancestor-symlink and post-receipt mutation tests that must fail."
    }
  ],
